Zero 0.12 guest files and Ztext validation
Date: 2026-11-17
Result: PASS, 280 terminal commands; all VM processes stopped.

Tested ISO SHA256:
386b4b3442ba47a939edb878d305327acc5df09378d85cbe595570d874b78312
Generated by the original Zero builder from current Zero/Ezero sources.

Boot matrix: BIOS64, BIOS32 (long mode and PAE disabled), UEFI64, UEFI32.
Each completed40 commands and a complete VM restart against its own private
ZeroFS disk. These are QEMU TCG serial-terminal tests, not a native VirtualBox
claim and not GUI/PS2 validation.

Verified on every boot path:
- Guest Zero create/save/readfile/writefile/del/watch/search/go/disks.
- Multiple filesystem requests in a single native guest program.
- Exclusive creation refuses overwrite; idempotent create preserves content.
- Missing-file failures, invalid text rejection, failed-read/list capacity
  leaves the caller buffer untouched, successful next command after errors.
- Exact-name search, wildcard *, single-character ?, empty results, NUL lists.
- Terminal search and del, current-root dot shorthand, invalid drive rejection.
- Ezero helpers, lists, and11 file operations in one expression, including
  one-based results and missing-file runtime error recovery.
- ZTEXT001 envelope validates exact length, reserved/header fields and FNV1a32
  before displaying the payload; damaged checksum and short header are errors.
- File creation/content/deletion and LF-containing Ztext survive a cold restart.

Foreign filesystem matrix: ext4, NTFS, Btrfs, each on BIOS64 and BIOS32.
Each completed18 commands and a complete restart on private copies of earlier
supported-profile fixtures. These are restricted profiles, not unrestricted
Windows/Linux filesystem compatibility. Guest programs created, wrote, read,
searched and deleted real on-disk files through the existing original drivers.
GO B:| changed the current terminal root after the program returned; subsequent
GO A:| demonstrated independent roots. Ezero multirequest and regular-file
listings passed. Ztext data containing LF also persisted on all three formats.

Rejected profiles: dirty ext4, NTFS with an unsupported initialized journal,
and default Btrfs outside the supported profile. Each refused create, save,
exclusive writefile and del; Ezero reported a runtime error and the next
program returned42. Complete private-volume SHA256 remained unchanged.

Implementation fixes validated during this work:
The guest continuation emitter now restores the fork return value before
entering the filesystem coroutine. Without it, the first request recursively
entered the app. Both64-bit and32-bit paths now resume the correct frame.
An empty terminal search now clears its query before the next prompt.
The native builder/BIOS/UEFI layout was adjusted for the enlarged32-bit kernel.

Scope and limits:
Shared-address-space cooperative applications, without memory isolation.
Flat ASCII names of1..31 bytes; file contents at most400 bytes, printable ASCII
plus TAB/LF/CR for writes. ZeroFS has eight slots. The filesystem profiles and
crash-recovery limits in fs/ remain applicable. Ztext's32-byte header leaves
at most368 payload bytes in guest files. The guest renderer rejects characters
outside its ASCII display subset; native zero-text supports validated UTF-8.
The whole-file program API returns raw bytes, including any Ztext envelope.

Protected user-owned media were never attached to these VMs or modified:
